# NPS logs from the Windows NPS server(s), read-only over SMB.
# 1) sudo apt-get install -y cifs-utils
# 2) Create a domain account with READ access to the NPS log share, e.g. \\NPS01\NPSLogs (C:\Windows\System32\LogFiles)
# 3) /etc/logsikka-smb.cred  (chmod 600, owner root):
#      username=svc-logsikka
#      password=...
#      domain=CORP
# 4) Add to /etc/fstab (one line per NPS server), then: sudo mkdir -p /mnt/nps/nps01 && sudo mount -a
//192.168.2.171/NPSLogs  /mnt/nps/nps01  cifs  ro,credentials=/etc/logsikka-smb.cred,uid=logsikka,gid=logsikka,file_mode=0440,dir_mode=0550,vers=3.0,nofail,x-systemd.automount  0  0
# 5) In Settings > NPS user mapping, set the folders to /mnt/nps/nps01 (one per line for several servers)
#    and uncomment RequiresMountsFor=/mnt/nps in /etc/systemd/system/logsikka.service, then daemon-reload.
# File offsets are stored per path, so the first read after the move starts from "On first start, read back (hours)".
